WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
A woman: ...7 in the book.

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Dr. Khalifa: Page 46.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:08.000
A woman: (unintelligible)

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Sura 92, The Night.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.000
In the name of GOD, Most Gracious, Most Merciful.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:25.000
[92:1] By the night as it covers. [92:2] The day as it reveals. [92:3] And Him who created the male and the female.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.000
[92:4] Your works are of various kinds.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.000
[92:5] As for him who gives to charity and maintains righteousness.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.000
[92:6] And upholds the scripture.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.000
[92:7] We will direct him towards happiness.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.000
[92:8] But he who is stingy, though he is rich.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.000
[92:9] And disbelieves in the scripture.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.000
[92:10] We will direct him towards misery.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.000
[92:11] His money cannot help him when he falls.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.000
[92:12] We provide the guidance.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.000
[92:13] We control the Hereafter, as well as this life.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.000
[92:14] I have warned you about the blazing Hellfire.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.000
[92:15] None burns therein except the wicked. [92:16] Who disbelieves and turns away.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.000
[92:17] Avoiding it will be the righteous. [92:18] Who gives from his money to charity.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.000
[92:19] Seeking nothing in return. [92:20] Seeking only his Lord, the Most High.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.000
[92:21] He will certainly attain salvation.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.000
Verse 1 and verse 2.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.000
[92:1] By the night as it covers. [92:2] The day as it reveals.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:22.000
There are many, many verses which refer to day, night, forenoon, and dawn.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.000
The night is created for our rest and therefore is a benefit.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:40.000
And we can use that as an analogy to this life because we're blocked from being in God's presence while we're in this life.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.000
It is a sort of darkness. It is a sort of barrier.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.000
We cannot stand God's presence in our present form.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.000
[92:2] The day as it reveals.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:58.000
Most of the references in Quran about day are about the Day of Resurrection all the way through.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:06.000
And I thought of that as an analogy to life which reveals the truth and things as they are.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:11.000
And I thought that appropriate too, when we consider the Day of Resurrection, the Day of Judgment,

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.000
because that's, in fact, what will happen.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:20.000
We're all familiar with this night and how black it can be without any stars or the moon out.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.000
I used to live up on a hill in the middle of the country and there was no electricity from house to house.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.000
There's nothing to see except the lightning bugs if you were fortunate.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.000
You couldn't see your hand in front of your face.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.000
It was that dark.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.000
And that's quite a cover.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:41.000
It removes our world from us so that what we remember of the world in the daylight really is an illusion.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:48.000
The night takes everything away and that's what happened to us when we had to come to this life.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:53.000
We had to be away from our real life for the period of time we're here.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:59.000
And when the sun comes up and things begin to take shape, the first thing that we see is silhouettes usually.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:05.000
I live across the street from a park now and when the sun rises, the trees don't have any texture or depth of color.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:08.000
They're shapes as the sun begins to come up.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.000
And they look flat.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:19.000
And as the sun rises further, the color appears and then its depth and texture and you see individual leaves moving and all the parts that make up the tree.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:25.000
And so the day is revelation and the Day of Judgment is a revelation to all of us,

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:30.000
even those of us who hope to be safe on the Day of Resurrection.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.000
I think we will also see things that we did not see ever in this lifetime.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:42.000
[92:3] And Him who created the male and the female. [92:4] Your works are of various kinds.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:50.000
Some time ago, I went through Quran and looked for all of the references that God made to the human being,

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:54.000
whether it was about creation or about our nature and our characters.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:04:01.000
And there are an awful lot, as I was telling Lydia before we started, an awful lot of descriptions of us

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:11.000
that are not real positive. We're hasty, we're unappreciative, contentious, parsimonious,

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:14.000
and unappreciative is throughout quite a bit.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:21.000
And there are rare instances where the verse might finish with the phrase "except for those who lead a righteous life" or something similar.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:31.000
Our works are of various kinds. And for those of us who do things that appear to be Quranic but we are still involved in idol worship,

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:36.000
we know that those works are nullified. And in fact, God designs those works to help others.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:44.000
We are all in the service of each other but that on the Day of Resurrection, if we are involved in idol worship, they will be as if we had not done them.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:56.000
Verses 5 through 11 describe two types of people.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:01.000
God alone knows what each of our choice was,

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:05.000
what in our hearts we really believe even though we forgot when we came here.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:16.000
For those of us who chose God alone, God willing all of us, God will give us everything in our life to augment that choice.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.000
We know those things as tests.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:23.000
We know them as gifts. We know them as miracles. We each have stories to tell.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:33.000
And as we recognize them as such, they augment and cement and increase our faith and our knowledge in God's truth and His guarantees.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:42.000
For those who do not believe, God also provides for them what they need to continue disbelief.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:47.000
It may appear as though they're wondrous things for instance they're very wealthy or people

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:53.000
that have great status or people that seem to have a lot of power and can get people

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:56.000
in countries to do things for themselves, for instance.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:00.000
Those people may consider themselves blessed, but God is merely continuing to test them

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:05.000
so that at the end, at the Day of Judgment, there will be no excuse whatsoever.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:11.000
Nothing they can say or do except to ask to come back and try again which, of course, we know will not be allowed.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:18.000
So, I read those verses as descriptions of how God is so Merciful to all of us

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:23.000
because even though God knows the choice of the disbelievers and augments that choice in their life,

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:28.000
He still is providing proof of God alone and the truth to them

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:33.000
in the midst of all the things that are given and all the things that seem to be provided so easily.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:43.000
What I thought was that I constantly think that this life is an illusion it is one huge test

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:54.000
for all of us, believers or not, and we have to keep striving to find the truth to be believers with certainty and that's very difficult.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:59.000
Sometimes some of the things that God causes to happen in our lives,

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:06.000
the people we meet, the settings we find ourselves in are confusing and they can make us wonder if we're on the right path at all.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:10.000
But that is in fact the test that we have to keep striving and stay

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:17.000
right where we're going toward God alone and whatever is puzzling will become clear very quickly if we do that.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:24.000
Does anybody have any comments, questions, additions, up till here?

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:31.000
Okay.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:36.000
[92:12] We provide the guidance.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:38.000
[92:13] We control the Hereafter, as well as this life.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.000
God controls all things.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:51.000
We speak of the words we utter, we think that they're our own, we think that the thoughts that we have are our own and we know that they aren't.

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:58.000
God knows ahead of time what we're going to say and the effect that our words are going to have on other people.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.000
More than that

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:08.000
[92:13] We control the Hereafter, as well as this life.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:11.000
Our lives are so perfectly designed.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:14.000
We have all the choices in the world available to us.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:19.000
What time we're going to get up for Salat in the morning, we choose that time

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:23.000
unless we wake up and don't need an alarm clock anymore like Rashad.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:28.000
We choose what we're gonna have for breakfast whether we're gonna eat at all.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:33.000
We choose how we're gonna get to work, we choose what time, we choose what we're going

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:37.000
to do when we get there, we choose how to prioritize the tasks in a day we think,

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:44.000
we have an awful lot of control over our lives, what we're going to wear, what we're going to do when we come home

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:49.000
that night, we make plans with the people in our lives, relatives, friends.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:55.000
All of that is designed for us. We have no choice at all in reality.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:09:02.000
All of that is a test and it's designed specifically, individually for each person in the world.

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:08.000
The money we earn is already predetermined. To worry about it is foolish.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:14.000
We know that God is Merciful and provides relief in every situation

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:20.000
including the amount of money that we need. And all of us have stories about some great need arising and not having

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:23.000
the faintest idea in the world how we were going to accomplish it, and

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:26.000
suddenly, there was money from somewhere unexplained.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:34.000
Our relatives, those people that are part of our family, mother, father, aunts, uncles, cousins, they were chosen for us also.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:42.000
For some of us, we are distanced from our family because of our choice to believe in God alone,

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:47.000
but that's also part of our test. We were assigned to their household as our children were assigned to our own.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:57.000
Those people that become friends of ours, those people that we find ourselves working with, whether we like them or not, were put there by God for us.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:03.000
I've talked before about working in a hospital and part of my job is to take care of patients.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:09.000
They're assigned a person like myself when they come into the hospital and we think that somebody

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:15.000
there assigns Joe Smith to Catherine, in fact God does that and allows me to meet

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:19.000
some people and not others that come through the hospital for a reason.

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:26.000
Material things that we gain or do not gain are again designed by God

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:35.000
to test whether we're focused on the need for those or not, amongst other things the environmental settings that we find ourselves in.

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:41.000
I remember traveling to the conference and Rashad telling that story about the bugs

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:46.000
at that time that we stopped to make Salat and made it the fastest we'd ever made it before.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:50.000
All of us were destined to do that. We didn't know that. We didn't know that was going to happen.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:55.000
And it was on green grass, as I remember, in the middle of the desert.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:11:00.000
It was a nice carpet of grass and Rashad was right where there was no grass. He just seemed to be waiting for all of us.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.000
He certainly was.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:07.000
But for some reason all of us were to share that experience and run

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:12.000
back to the van, I remember going back to the van. We didn't stay there very long.

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:19.000
All the things that are designed in our lives whether they're people or things or places we travel to, they're all designed

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:25.000
by God. And in all of them is the proof of God alone and that God controls all things.

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:34.000
If we are truly searching for that, we'll see that in all things, in all conversations, in all the people that we meet, all the places that we go.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:40.000
If we know that God controls everything and there are layers and layers of that.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:45.000
When we first begin to understand that God controls everything, it's confusing

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:52.000
because you wanna say "well, wait a minute, I, I chose that and I chose this" and, and then, the realization comes

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:59.000
that God controls everything and you didn't choose it. But you still retain the thought that what's in your head is your own.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.000
Out there is ok, God's running all of that,

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:08.000
but your thoughts are your own and you're using your mind to understand that and then the next layer peels away

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:11.000
and you realize that the thoughts you have in your head are not even your own.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:16.000
They're part of a perfectly designed life for each of us. And in those lives, the truth is buried

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:21.000
everywhere. In fact, it's not buried, it's so obvious and the more layers we peel away and

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:25.000
the more understanding we come to have about the reason we're here and what God is doing

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:31.000
for us in His Great Mercy and Graciousness to us, it becomes as if everything floats to

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:34.000
the surface. The world looks very very different.

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:37.000
Jason just bought a car and I was telling Rashad

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:43.000
this the other day, he had to buy it because it had a big 19 all over it but that's another story.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:46.000
And we were talking about him driving on the road with him being just 16,

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:52.000
his mother saying to myself "I really hope God means it when He says He's gonna protect everybody" from Jason.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:56.000
And we were talking, and we were talking and I said

00:12:56.000 --> 00:13:02.000
"you know, I often drive to work and I think of all of the things, the creatures that are driving along with me."

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:10.000
It's not just the cars as bumper to bumper, but it's every person in every car has a jinn riding with them

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:15.000
and two angels one on the right and one on the left, and it's a wonder there's any room on the road for the car,

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:20.000
when you think about that, but all those other people driving along looking right and left as if they don't know that.

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:27.000
They've no idea how much protection is involved in those near misses when somebody turns left and we can see the angel right there.

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:31.000
We can't, but we can, we know the angel was there to avoid this crash.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:37.000
So, world takes on a very different perspective and, Alhamdu Lillah, a great peace occurs

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:42.000
when we understand that what seems bad is in that God is after us in Mercy

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:50.000
and to provide the guidance that we need to find Him and return to Him and never be separated again it's really incredible.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:54.000
A woman: Are there any comments about those two verses?

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:58.000
Dr. Khalifa: Finish the Sura.

00:13:58.000 --> 00:13:58.000
A woman: No.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.000
Dr. Khalifa: You're doing so well.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:03.000
A woman: Rashad, you have any comments at all?

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:04.000
Dr. Khalifa: You finished.

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:05.000
A woman: Yes.

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:07.000
A woman: Ok.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:11.000
[92:14] I have warned you about the blazing Hellfire. [92:15] None burns therein except the wicked.

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:14.000
[92:16] Who disbelieves and turns away.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:20.000
That's very straight forward. God gives many descriptions in Quran about the types of people that are going to end up in Hell.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:28.000
And some of them are almost abstract. This is very straight forward and it's a bottom line.

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:32.000
People who disbelieve and turn away are wicked and there is no second chance.

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:39.000
Hell is where these people will be and they don't know it. They won't know it until the Day of Resurrection.

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:43.000
[92:17] Avoiding it will be the righteous.

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:46.000
[92:18] Who gives from his money to charity. [92:19] Seeking nothing in return.

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:48.000
[92:20] ... only his Lord, the Most High.

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:51.000
[92:21] He will certainly attain salvation.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:56.000
The righteous are spared with the greatest mercy because we know that we've all sinned.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:15:06.000
For those of us who mercifully come to understand God alone and free ourselves from any type of idol worship including our own ego,

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:14.000
this is a tremendous accomplishment. It's described as such with words in Quran but I don't think we can fully understand

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:23.000
how much mercy from God is involved here for us to escape even to end up in Purgatory hanging on by our toenails would be an incredible mercy.

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:32.000
And then, God again very simply describes those people who are going to avoid Hell for all eternity

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:39.000
and those are people who are not really attached to this world, who understand that what is part of their life

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:42.000
is, is given. It is all a gift from God.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:50.000
And it is not meant that we should keep every single thing that comes our way and to think of anything as ours

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:57.000
is also foolish because it's God's. And if we're meant to give it away then we should do that without ever looking back.

00:15:57.000 --> 00:16:05.000
One of the difficulties I had in my family being raised as a Christian, we had to go through that Christmas fantasy that happens for months every year.

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:11.000
And in my family from the time I was very young, the giving of gifts never was the giving of gifts,

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:16.000
it was always attached to conditions even though everyone knew, for instance, that

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:20.000
we had three small children and didn't have a lot of money and the gifts were given with

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:26.000
great smiles, there was always the great frown and the comments that similar gifts were not given in return.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:33.000
And if they weren't, it was remembered from year to year to year to year, forever.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:38.000
And finally, long before I moved to Tucson, Alhamdu Lillah, I just told my family

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:42.000
"we don't do Christmas anymore. I don't know what it is anymore. I don't know what you think you're doing,

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:46.000
"but I cannot participate in it. I cannot encourage my children to do this."

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:51.000
This is, this is just horrible. You don't know how to give anything. My family would come to help,

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:56.000
and the help was more of a burden because there were strings attached to that, something that we were,

00:16:56.000 --> 00:17:02.000
we were supposed to do or behave or perform. God says that for those of us who are

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:08.000
true believers, we recognize that, that what we have is to be shared with the people around us,

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:15.000
because it's given to us for that purpose to overcome our natural need to be

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:20.000
stingy and to hoard is also a tremendous accomplishment. It's almost impossible.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:31.000
I was in the, finally up in the DeGrazia Gallery, recently. I didn't know where it was and hadn't heard of this man forever.

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:35.000
And a guest came down from Phoenix and she had wanted to go, so we drove up there,

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:40.000
walked around in the last 20 minutes of the day and there are pictures on the wall, I don't know

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:45.000
how many of you have been up there, some of them are the little girls, the Indian girls

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:48.000
that we all recognize as DeGrazia's work but he did a lot of other things so there's

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:52.000
oil paintings on the wall and so are the prices of these paintings.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:18:01.000
And I cannot imagine someone paying $2,000 for a painting never mind more than that and there were many for $2,000 $4,000.

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:07.000
And as Lisa walked around, at one point, I heard her, we were alone, it was almost toward the end of it, closing.

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:10.000
And she, she put her hands on her hips and she looked in the glass display

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:15.000
case also with items, price tags attached and said to herself

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:22.000
"I would hope that if I had that much money, I would give it to charity and I would not buy this painting or this (unintelligible)."

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:31.000
And I looked at her and I thought "dead on, she doesn't know much about Islam, but that's the way we need to be.

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:39.000
"To have that kind of money and not think about using it to help others is a sin." And there are many people like that as we know.

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:50.000
The last two verses tell us what we get and God always gives a guarantee, seeking only our Lord, the Most High.

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:59.000
If we stay focused on that and not this material world, accepting so far as we are to behave righteously and we are giving guidelines for that,

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:09.000
he will certainly obtain salvation. This is a guarantee. There's no question at all. And there are many such guarantees in Quran,

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:15.000
if we but follow God's instructions. The path can at times seem extraordinarily narrow

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:22.000
and at other times so wide because we feel so protected, those angels seem to grow before our eyes.

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:29.000
Fortunately, we don't try to fly without wings, but it's almost that wonderful, that kind of peace.

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:33.000
And then the tests come again as the purification process continues.

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:43.000
If we stay focused on God alone and we manage to pass those tests, that we are sincere in our hearts, Salvation means eternal life, or we're alive.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:51.000
There's nothing that we could possibly want in this world that's more than that, or better than that or equal to it.

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:55.000
A woman: Now, does anybody have comments?

