Dr. Khalifa: Contrasts.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:11.000
Edip: Yes.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:23.000
A man: Why the contrast? Why did not (unintelligible)

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:29.000
Edip: (unintelligible). Our life is based on contrast.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:34.000
Everything we can see, there is opposite.

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:45.000
And by this struggle between the opposite things, or changing, rotation between the opposite things, we see life, everything,

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:57.000
days, and nights, (unintelligible), beautiful, ugly, small, big, everything we can... poverty, (unintelligible).

00:21:57.000 --> 00:22:13.000
Edip: And if we can see a good person, a bad person, a good person life, a day, a bad person life, night (unintelligible).

00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:15.000
Edip: (unintelligible) A man: (unintelligible)

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:25.000
A man: I have a question. Why the three first, first three verses, our God is swearing

00:22:25.000 --> 00:22:27.000
[92:1] By the night ...

00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:29.000
[92:2] The day ...

00:22:29.000 --> 00:22:31.000
[92:3] And ... male and ... female.

00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:32.000
(unintelligible)

00:22:32.000 --> 00:22:34.000
[92:4] Your works are of various kinds.

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:46.000
Why, why three verses, God is swearing to these three, although they are coming in contrast,

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:49.000
(unintelligible)

00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:52.000
creation, life, and being.

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:58.000
It doesn't matter if you have (unintelligible) anything. Then,

00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:02.000
[92:4] Your works are of various kinds.

00:23:02.000 --> 00:23:05.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yeah, we have three. We have three profound introductions.

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:11.000
Dr. Khalifa: The day and the night are profound signs, as you know.

00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:19.000
They remind us that the earth is hanging in space, and the male and the female.

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:26.000
So, these three profound verses tell us that... actually, this short Sura tells the secret of happiness.

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:33.000
So, it is very important to know which path will lead you to happiness, in this world and forever,

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:36.000
and which path will lead you to misery, in this world and forever.

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:42.000
So, you see in verse 7, the path to happiness.

00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:49.000
Sura 54, if you remember, God says, He directs you to happiness or misery. He controls that.

00:23:50.000 --> 00:23:53.000
It is now established that material success does not bring happiness.

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:56.000
So,

00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:58.000
[92:4] Your works are of various kinds.

00:23:58.000 --> 00:24:03.000
And they will lead you to either path, happiness or misery.

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:10.000
And what I wanted to emphasize is verses 5 and 18. Both of them talk about charity.

00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:19.000
In this short Sura, two verses talk about charity, because it's a continuous process.

00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:26.000
Just like we feed, God wants to remind us that, just because we continuously feed our body, how many times did you drink today?

00:24:27.000 --> 00:24:31.000
You drank water or coke or something today.

00:24:31.000 --> 00:24:37.000
You drank, you ate, you really take care of your body, your garment.

00:24:38.000 --> 00:24:41.000
So, God is reminding us to take care of the real person, of you.

00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:48.000
To take care of you is a continuous process, just like the eating, and the drinking, and the sleeping,

00:24:48.000 --> 00:24:57.000
and the showering, the things that you do for your body, is a continuous process, and like the five Contact Prayers,

00:24:57.000 --> 00:25:02.000
continuous process, Charity also is a continuous process, because you continuously make money.

00:25:03.000 --> 00:25:11.000
You have to set aside 2.5% for your relatives, your parents, and so on, as the Quran directs.

00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:21.000
The three verses, three profound signs, this is common in the short Suras, precede something that's very important.

00:25:22.000 --> 00:25:25.000
And here, the important thing is the secret of happiness.

00:25:27.000 --> 00:25:34.000
Dr. Khalifa: If you do these continuous processes, that develop your soul, God promises you, happiness now and forever.

00:25:35.000 --> 00:25:41.000
Edip: So, these three verses are consistent with the, with the text, because in verse 4,

00:25:41.000 --> 00:25:44.000
[92:4] Your works are of various kinds.

00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:45.000
Dr. Khalifa: Contrasting.

00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:50.000
Edip: Yes, (unintelligible)

00:25:50.000 --> 00:25:56.000
Edip: And then, the Hereafter (unintelligible).

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:11.000
A man: Why, why (unintelligible) charity (unintelligible)

00:26:11.000 --> 00:26:12.000
Dr. Khalifa: Because people neglect to do it.

00:26:14.000 --> 00:26:18.000
Dr. Khalifa: It's not only in this Sura. Actually, if you look in almost every Sura, you see it.

00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:28.000
Edip: Especially, Rashad, especially in Meccan Suras, chapters, in short chapters, you can find...

00:26:28.000 --> 00:26:30.000
Dr. Khalifa: In almost every Sura, we have something about charity.

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:36.000
Edip: But in short chapters, the average percentage of the charity is more.

00:26:43.000 --> 00:26:46.000
Dr. Khalifa: It's something that people tend to forget, to neglect.

00:26:47.000 --> 00:26:50.000
In fact, I keep repeating, so I remind myself.

00:26:51.000 --> 00:26:56.000
I need to remind myself, not to be lax in doing it.

00:26:57.000 --> 00:27:00.000
So every time, we receive money, we just have to cut out 2.5%.

00:27:02.000 --> 00:27:03.000
It's a very good investment.

00:27:03.000 --> 00:27:09.000
The reason God repeats it is because God knows that we tend to forget, or neglect to do it.

00:27:13.000 --> 00:27:15.000
We seem to do the five daily Prayers easily.

00:27:17.000 --> 00:27:23.000
Charity is something that we tend to forget, because we get involved in spending. Before you know it, your money is gone.

00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:26.000
We didn't set aside the 2.5%.

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:37.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, the reason this is... also, repetition is, is psychologically important.

00:27:39.000 --> 00:27:41.000
A man: (unintelligible) This is a comment.

00:27:42.000 --> 00:27:52.000
A man: Since God knows the human being (unintelligible), we're Praying, we Pray because, you know, it doesn't cost you anything.

00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:56.000
A man: (unintelligible)

00:27:57.000 --> 00:28:12.000
A man: But giving money, (unintelligible)

00:28:12.000 --> 00:28:16.000
Dr. Khalifa: Also, it has to be a continuous process just like eating and drinking.

00:28:18.000 --> 00:28:20.000
Dr. Khalifa: (unintelligible)

00:28:20.000 --> 00:28:24.000
A woman: (unintelligible), in looking up about charity (unintelligible)

00:28:24.000 --> 00:28:28.000
the verse, the verse (unintelligible) in chapter 2

00:28:28.000 --> 00:28:32.000
say that you give from the money you earned.

00:28:32.000 --> 00:28:42.000
A woman: Does that mean, say, if you're given money that you didn't work for? I know it would be better if you gave from it, but do you have to give?

00:28:42.000 --> 00:28:43.000
A woman: (unintelligible)

00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:48.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yeah, any money you earn, you earn whether you work for it or not, any money that you make.

00:28:49.000 --> 00:28:52.000
Dr. Khalifa: Any money that enters your pocket and becomes yours.

00:28:57.000 --> 00:28:59.000
Dr. Khalifa: Anybody else? Questions? 93.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:01.000
A man: (unintelligible)

00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:01.000
Dr. Khalifa: Hmm?

00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:03.000
A man: If you loan money...

00:29:03.000 --> 00:29:03.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:29:03.000 --> 00:29:05.000
A man: (unintelligible)

00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:10.000
Dr. Khalifa: The loan money is supposed to happen during (unintelligible).

00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:20.000
Dr. Khalifa: In other words, you receive $500, you take 2.5%, and then somebody wants $300, you will loan the $300, your $300 is already purified.

00:29:21.000 --> 00:29:23.000
The money is purified only once.

00:29:24.000 --> 00:29:25.000
Dr. Khalifa: Who's waving here? Hi!

00:29:27.000 --> 00:29:31.000
A woman: Do people have to pay charity money on charity money (unintelligible)?

00:29:31.000 --> 00:29:32.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:29:33.000 --> 00:29:38.000
Dr. Khalifa: Because, because every person knows some, some other people who will need assistance.

00:29:39.000 --> 00:29:41.000
It is based on personal knowledge.

00:29:43.000 --> 00:29:49.000
This is why God gave you that sequence, your parents, your relatives, the orphans, the poor, the needy, the alien.

00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:55.000
It's based on personal knowledge.

00:29:56.000 --> 00:30:02.000
And we read in Sura 2 that there are people who may need it and nobody will know.

00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:04.000
Dr. Khalifa: But people close to them will know. Go ahead.

00:30:04.000 --> 00:30:12.000
A woman: But (unintelligible)

00:30:12.000 --> 00:30:17.000
A woman: I was at work (unintelligible)

00:30:17.000 --> 00:30:25.000
a phone call (unintelligible) this person that was (unintelligible) person

00:30:25.000 --> 00:30:30.000
(unintelligible) for a whole day. (unintelligible)

00:30:31.000 --> 00:30:37.000
A woman: It was (unintelligible) and it was right (unintelligible)

00:30:38.000 --> 00:30:40.000
Dr. Khalifa: But God was helping you. Yes. A woman: Yes.

00:30:42.000 --> 00:30:44.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, (unintelligible). It's based on personal knowledge.

00:30:48.000 --> 00:30:50.000
Dr. Khalifa: Sura 93, (unintelligible)

00:30:50.000 --> 00:30:51.000
A woman: (unintelligible)

00:30:51.000 --> 00:30:54.000
[93:3] Your Lord never abandoned you, nor did He forget.

00:30:55.000 --> 00:30:58.000
[93:4] The Hereafter is far better for you than this first (life).

00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:02.000
[93:5] And your Lord will give you enough; you will be pleased.

00:31:03.000 --> 00:31:05.000
[93:6] Did He not find you orphaned and He gave you a home?

00:31:06.000 --> 00:31:08.000
[93:7] He found you astray, and guided you.

00:31:08.000 --> 00:31:11.000
[93:8] He found you poor, and made you rich.

00:31:11.000 --> 00:31:14.000
[93:9] Therefore, you shall not forsake the orphan.

00:31:14.000 --> 00:31:16.000
[93:10] Nor shall you reprimand the beggar.

00:31:16.000 --> 00:31:20.000
[93:11] You shall proclaim the blessing your Lord has bestowed upon you.

00:31:21.000 --> 00:31:30.000
It seems to be almost a repetition, and again, preceded by the same profound phrases.

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:30.000
[93:1] By the forenoon.

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:33.000
which is the brightest part of the day, and

00:31:33.000 --> 00:31:34.000
[93:2] By the night as it falls.

00:31:34.000 --> 00:31:36.000
[93:3] Your Lord never abandoned you, ...

00:31:38.000 --> 00:31:42.000
Closer to us than our jugular vein is the phrase that all of us remember.

00:31:42.000 --> 00:31:46.000
We have constant companions recording but also protecting us.

00:31:48.000 --> 00:31:54.000
Psalm 91 talks about the angels protecting us lest we dash our foot against a stone.

00:31:57.000 --> 00:32:03.000
There's a popular kind of poem, I guess, it's called Footprints that You See Out,

00:32:03.000 --> 00:32:10.000
and the man questions why in the worst part of his life he only saw one set of footprints in the sand,

00:32:10.000 --> 00:32:17.000
and was almost accusing God of not keeping His promise, that God lets him get all of that out and then says,

00:32:17.000 --> 00:32:20.000
those were the times that I carried you.

00:32:21.000 --> 00:32:26.000
I think that's directed at Jesus and I can't remember now but the truth of it is profound.

00:32:26.000 --> 00:32:31.000
We are never alone in the worst of times ever and we are protected.

00:32:31.000 --> 00:32:34.000
Edip never once got stopped by a policeman on that trip.

00:32:35.000 --> 00:32:36.000
We are protected.

00:32:36.000 --> 00:32:38.000
Even, even something like that.

00:32:38.000 --> 00:32:40.000
I mean, that just was amazing.

00:32:44.000 --> 00:32:46.000
[93:4] The Hereafter is far better for you than this first (life).

00:32:46.000 --> 00:32:48.000
The Hereafter is our quest.

00:32:49.000 --> 00:32:52.000
There are so many stories and movies that are what I call quest movies.

00:32:52.000 --> 00:33:01.000
There's always some goal to be strived for and great sacrifices and great dangers on the way to the prize, whatever it may be.

00:33:03.000 --> 00:33:04.000
But that's what we're doing.

00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:11.000
Our whole lives are a quest and there are great dangers and many distractions and many provisions along the way.

00:33:13.000 --> 00:33:19.000
We have to remember that this life is not the goal, and that's very hard.

00:33:19.000 --> 00:33:24.000
There are so many distractions in our day. So many. A phone call.

00:33:24.000 --> 00:33:30.000
Just as you're starting to think about what to do with the (unintelligible) for that week, you get a phone call. The beeper goes off.

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:34.000
Somebody comes in your office. Somebody calls you and the thought goes.

00:33:34.000 --> 00:33:36.000
And it doesn't come back maybe for hours.

00:33:36.000 --> 00:33:39.000
And you have to say "who was your god for that day?"

00:33:39.000 --> 00:33:44.000
"How many minutes did you retain that thought throughout all the things that you do during the day?"

00:33:44.000 --> 00:33:50.000
Our quest is to focus on getting ourselves safely to the Hereafter to be with God.

00:33:53.000 --> 00:33:54.000
And a guarantee.

00:33:54.000 --> 00:33:57.000
[93:5] And your Lord will give you enough; you will be pleased.

00:33:58.000 --> 00:34:00.000
I have no idea what that means.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:03.000
I have absolutely no idea what that means.

00:34:03.000 --> 00:34:08.000
A woman: I have so much that's enough in my life. Everything. I have enough of everything right now.

00:34:08.000 --> 00:34:10.000
Dr. Khalifa: But this is it. This is what it means.

00:34:11.000 --> 00:34:13.000
A woman: But enough in the Hereafter.

00:34:14.000 --> 00:34:15.000
Dr. Khalifa: No, this is here.

00:34:16.000 --> 00:34:17.000
Dr. Khalifa: (unintelligible)

00:34:17.000 --> 00:34:21.000
A woman: And in the Hereafter. I mean, the two things are incomprehensible to us.

00:34:21.000 --> 00:34:23.000
[93:5] ... you will be pleased.

00:34:23.000 --> 00:34:24.000
is an understatement.

00:34:27.000 --> 00:34:30.000
And then, the question we were discussing a moment ago.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:32.000
[93:6] Did He not find you orphaned ... gave you a home?

00:34:32.000 --> 00:34:33.000
[93:7] ... astray, and guided you.

00:34:33.000 --> 00:34:34.000
[93:8] ... poor, and made you rich.

00:34:35.000 --> 00:34:37.000
God provides for all creatures.

00:34:37.000 --> 00:34:42.000
Rashad talked about the sunflowers and the ants that crawl under them. And the alligators in Florida.

00:34:43.000 --> 00:34:48.000
All of them with hearts beating. All of them needing food, nutrients. The system is incredible.

00:34:48.000 --> 00:34:51.000
It is such a complex interlocking system,

00:34:51.000 --> 00:34:56.000
right down to the tiniest cell and its components, which we are down to quarks at this point.

00:34:56.000 --> 00:34:59.000
Everything has its provisions.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:02.000
We don't know how to do that. We're still...

00:35:02.000 --> 00:35:08.000
I drove the other day to work and there was a young man setting up a tripod with a surveying instrument on it.

00:35:09.000 --> 00:35:13.000
And I watched him. He was walking, walking down the road,

00:35:13.000 --> 00:35:16.000
not flying in a jet convoy, but still walking with a tripod,

00:35:16.000 --> 00:35:20.000
the same kind of, I don't know, George Washington used or Galileo used,

00:35:20.000 --> 00:35:24.000
peering through a tube to establish a straight eye

00:35:24.000 --> 00:35:27.000
And I thought, we've come so far and we've done nothing.

00:35:27.000 --> 00:35:29.000
We've just done nothing. We're still walking.

00:35:29.000 --> 00:35:31.000
We're, we're still walking.

00:35:31.000 --> 00:35:38.000
Surely, there's another way from a satellite or something to do what he had to do by walking and setting up this awkward instrument.

00:35:39.000 --> 00:35:41.000
Provisions for all things.

00:35:43.000 --> 00:35:45.000
[93:9] Therefore, you shall not forsake the orphan.

00:35:45.000 --> 00:35:48.000
[93:10] Nor shall you reprimand the beggar.

00:35:48.000 --> 00:35:51.000
[93:11] You shall proclaim the blessing your Lord has bestowed upon you.

00:35:51.000 --> 00:35:57.000
There's a Sura, I'm sorry I don't know the number where Muhammad is told not to ignore

00:35:57.000 --> 00:36:05.000
those that come to him that appear not to be perhaps as wealthy or as well-situated as others.

00:36:05.000 --> 00:36:12.000
I think he was chastised for ignoring a person like that and tending to someone else over him.

00:36:12.000 --> 00:36:15.000
We don't know other people's choices.

00:36:16.000 --> 00:36:22.000
We have no idea what their eventual choice, their eventual place is going to be in the Eternal Life.

00:36:22.000 --> 00:36:24.000
And it's not for us to judge.

00:36:24.000 --> 00:36:30.000
It is for us to forsake the material world and hence our own egos, our own bodies

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:39.000
that we pay so much attention to and take care of the world around us. For all we know these are our family, our real family.

00:36:39.000 --> 00:36:42.000
And we wouldn't know that. We have no way of knowing that.

00:36:44.000 --> 00:36:47.000
[93:11] You shall proclaim the blessing your Lord has bestowed upon you.

00:36:47.000 --> 00:36:49.000
Mã Shã Allãh. Alhamdu Lillah.

00:36:50.000 --> 00:36:51.000
IN SHAA ALLAH.

00:36:52.000 --> 00:37:00.000
Be careful how we speak of God. It came to mind because Rashad talked to us one day about

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:02.000
being careful how we spoke about God.

00:37:02.000 --> 00:37:03.000
God does not make us sick.

00:37:04.000 --> 00:37:06.000
We make ourselves sick. God heals.

00:37:08.000 --> 00:37:11.000
We used, I think you used this example of Moses and his teacher.

00:37:11.000 --> 00:37:18.000
And each one of those examples, it was the human being that made the error and God that made it right.

00:37:18.000 --> 00:37:21.000
So, we need to proclaim God's blessing to us.

00:37:21.000 --> 00:37:26.000
We don't need to say to each other "well, God made that tire flat" and leave it there.

00:37:26.000 --> 00:37:31.000
We need to understand what we're saying. We need to be real careful. If the tire's flat, we did something.

00:37:32.000 --> 00:37:35.000
God will help us get the tire fixed so the car will go again.

00:37:36.000 --> 00:37:40.000
And it really is that simple and that complex at the same time.

00:37:40.000 --> 00:37:43.000
Words come out of our mouths very quickly. We don't think about them.

00:37:44.000 --> 00:37:46.000
Sometimes we just speak.

00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:52.000
And we need to be careful. I've taught myself any number of times after that (unintelligible)

00:37:52.000 --> 00:37:59.000
stopping in the middle of a sentence or a word and rephrasing it because we understand that God runs and controls all things.

00:37:59.000 --> 00:38:02.000
He allows the things to happen that need to happen for us.

00:38:02.000 --> 00:38:08.000
So, it's very easy to make a mistake, cross over the line and say "I'm sick because God wanted me to be sick for this reason."

00:38:09.000 --> 00:38:10.000
That's not it.

00:38:11.000 --> 00:38:17.000
So, we need to be very careful and only talk about the good things that God does.

00:38:20.000 --> 00:38:21.000
Comments?

