00:45:57.000 --> 00:46:00.000
Dr. Khalifa: Right. You don't attribute sickness to God.

00:46:01.000 --> 00:46:05.000
Dr. Khalifa: You don't attribute sickness to God. You attribute it to yourself. Say "I did something wrong."

00:46:05.000 --> 00:46:06.000
A woman: Cause I put...

00:46:06.000 --> 00:46:07.000
Dr. Khalifa: God is teaching you. A woman: (unintelligible)

00:46:07.000 --> 00:46:11.000
A woman: ...because of diseases. I mean like, because of (unintelligible) consequences.

00:46:12.000 --> 00:46:17.000
A woman: For instance, like, I was really sick the other day. I was really sick.

00:46:18.000 --> 00:46:23.000
And the next day, I was feeling, I mean, so much better. I was fine.

00:46:24.000 --> 00:46:27.000
And (unintelligible) I was sick, I (unintelligible)

00:46:27.000 --> 00:46:30.000
A woman: And then the following day, (unintelligible), I mean, the thought of (unintelligible).

00:46:31.000 --> 00:46:39.000
A woman: ...And was told that sometimes it's to make us more appreciative for all those days, year after year, that we get up and we feel fine.

00:46:40.000 --> 00:46:46.000
All those days that we can eat every meal and it stays down, in me a lot more than in others.

00:46:48.000 --> 00:46:53.000
We don't think about that. We take that for granted. We get very caught up in our lives.

00:46:53.000 --> 00:46:57.000
And we just swing our feet out of bed and go to it in the morning.

