00:48:24.000 --> 00:48:26.000
Dr. Khalifa: 94: Cooling the Temper

00:48:26.000 --> 00:48:28.000
Mahmoud: I have a question. Dr. Khalifa: Go, Mahmoud.

00:48:29.000 --> 00:48:34.000
Mahmoud: In Sura (unintelligible) Muhammad.

00:48:35.000 --> 00:48:44.000
Dr. Khalifa: OK, I'm glad you brought this up. Some people think that this Sura was directed to Muhammad personally because of

00:48:44.000 --> 00:48:45.000
[93:5] ... your Lord will give you ...

00:48:46.000 --> 00:48:49.000
[93:6] Did He not find you orphaned and He gave you a home?

00:48:49.000 --> 00:48:50.000
Because Muhammad is an orphan.

00:48:51.000 --> 00:48:54.000
[93:7] He found you astray, and He guided you.

00:48:55.000 --> 00:48:59.000
You will not get the Muhammadans to confess that he ever was astray.

00:49:03.000 --> 00:49:13.000
(unintelligible) is laughing because I had my father, he was for four months here and I, I wanted him to say "Muhammad was astray" and he wouldn't say it.

00:49:15.000 --> 00:49:17.000
We had lots of funny encounters.

00:49:17.000 --> 00:49:21.000
Because when I showed him all the other verses showing that Muhammad did make mistakes,

00:49:21.000 --> 00:49:25.000
he will say "OK, so he was astray."

00:49:25.000 --> 00:49:27.000
And then five minutes later, he changes his mind.

00:49:29.000 --> 00:49:30.000
So we...

00:49:31.000 --> 00:49:39.000
The way he said "OK, he was astray", but became... something that would make us laugh every time we remember.

00:49:40.000 --> 00:49:45.000
But anyway, "He found you and..." they will not agree that he was astray.

00:49:45.000 --> 00:49:48.000
So, I chose to make the translation general.

00:49:50.000 --> 00:49:53.000
[93:8] He found you poor, and He made you rich.

00:49:54.000 --> 00:49:56.000
Because it's applicable to everybody.

00:49:56.000 --> 00:49:59.000
If they want to apply it... ironically, most of them...

00:49:59.000 --> 00:50:05.000
almost all of them apply to Muhammad, but they will not accept verse 7.

00:50:07.000 --> 00:50:12.000
Dr. Khalifa: In almost all the Tafseer interpretations, they interpret this Sura as if God is talking to Muhammad only.

00:50:13.000 --> 00:50:19.000
Edip: They misinterpret this verse, verse 7, a problem, a very big problem for them

00:50:19.000 --> 00:50:20.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:50:20.000 --> 00:50:26.000
Edip: because their idol becomes, before prophethood, he was astray.

00:50:26.000 --> 00:50:32.000
And then, they want to interpret, one of the most famous interpretations is,

00:50:32.000 --> 00:50:37.000
Edip: "he when, when he was a child, he lost his way (unintelligible)."

00:50:38.000 --> 00:50:40.000
Dr. Khalifa: What does it say (unintelligible)

00:50:40.000 --> 00:50:45.000
Mahmoud: That's exactly what Rashad says that he was poor and God made him rich.

00:50:45.000 --> 00:50:47.000
Mahmoud: That's exactly what (unintelligible).

00:50:48.000 --> 00:50:50.000
Edip: (93:7) وَوَجَدَكَ ضَآلًّۭا فَهَدَىٰ

00:50:50.000 --> 00:50:53.000
Edip: They say "But he lost his way when he was a child."

00:50:53.000 --> 00:51:01.000
Mahmoud: How (unintelligible).

00:51:01.000 --> 00:51:04.000
Edip: Also, a very short translation, this is the reason.

00:51:04.000 --> 00:51:05.000
Mahmoud: No.

00:51:05.000 --> 00:51:06.000
Edip: (unintelligible)

00:51:06.000 --> 00:51:08.000
Audience: (unintelligible)

00:51:10.000 --> 00:51:17.000
A woman: Also, you know, all of us will be orphan at one time or another, unless we die before our parents do.

00:51:17.000 --> 00:51:20.000
A woman: But God always provides the home.

00:51:25.000 --> 00:51:37.000
Mahmoud: The reason I'm saying this is that, (unintelligible) that Sura that we have, Cooling the Temper, (unintelligible)

00:51:37.000 --> 00:51:44.000
of Muhammad, and all the Suras together (unintelligible)

00:51:44.000 --> 00:51:48.000
Mahmoud: Sura that (unintelligible)

00:51:48.000 --> 00:51:50.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, (unintelligible)

00:51:51.000 --> 00:51:53.000
Also, the next Sura, you do the same thing.

00:51:54.000 --> 00:51:55.000
But it can apply to everyone.

00:51:56.000 --> 00:52:01.000
Because when you attain... the next Sura, I'm sorry, I'm going to the next one, it says,

00:52:01.000 --> 00:52:03.000
[94:1] Did we not cool your temper?

00:52:03.000 --> 00:52:12.000
This can apply to any believer, because before belief, we were excitable, and worries, we were worried, and...

00:52:12.000 --> 00:52:17.000
But when you believe, then you put your trust in God, and you submit, submit to God.

00:52:17.000 --> 00:52:22.000
And as submitters, we realize that God knows what is best for us, and we put everything in God's hands.

00:52:22.000 --> 00:52:25.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, we don't worry anymore and you cool your temper.

00:52:25.000 --> 00:52:27.000
A man: (unintelligible)

00:52:27.000 --> 00:52:30.000
Dr. Khalifa: It's, it's, you find that it is not worth it to get angry.

00:52:31.000 --> 00:52:34.000
There's nothing in this world that is worth getting angry at.

00:52:38.000 --> 00:52:43.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, this can be also general. So, we go to Catherine and Sura 94.

00:52:45.000 --> 00:52:48.000
Catherine: In the name of GOD, Most Gracious, Most Merciful.

00:52:48.000 --> 00:52:50.000
[94:1] Did we not cool your temper?

00:52:50.000 --> 00:52:52.000
[94:2] And we unloaded your load (of sins).

00:52:52.000 --> 00:52:54.000
[94:3] One that burdened your back.

00:52:54.000 --> 00:52:57.000
[94:4] We exalted you to an honorable position.

00:52:57.000 --> 00:53:02.000
[94:5] With pain there is gain. [94:6] Indeed, with pain there is gain.

00:53:02.000 --> 00:53:06.000
[94:7] Whenever possible you shall strive. [94:8] Seeking only your Lord.

00:53:11.000 --> 00:53:17.000
To paraphrase just a little bit on what Rashad said, although that is the bottom line,

00:53:17.000 --> 00:53:22.000
there's nothing in this world that should cause us to be emotionally involved with it to the point where we're angry.

00:53:22.000 --> 00:53:26.000
But even annoyance, a little bit of suspicion.

00:53:26.000 --> 00:53:31.000
I remember Rashad giving us the example of walking past someone on the street, and the

00:53:31.000 --> 00:53:35.000
person seemed to be making a face, and we thought "that person doesn't like me."

00:53:36.000 --> 00:53:37.000
That's wrong.

00:53:37.000 --> 00:53:39.000
How do we know they don't have a stomachache?

00:53:42.000 --> 00:53:47.000
That's helped me a lot in my dealings with other people, and I work in a place where

00:53:47.000 --> 00:53:53.000
I see an awful lot of people who are troubled, and if I was to, to make,

00:53:53.000 --> 00:54:00.000
to be concerned that, perhaps, they didn't like me, or they didn't wanna talk to me, I mean, I, I just, I wouldn't go there at all.

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:02.000
It would be very easy to misinterpret.

00:54:03.000 --> 00:54:09.000
On the other hand, if I understand that this person is part of the family of God,

00:54:09.000 --> 00:54:15.000
that I don't know this person's choice, but that they are to be treated the same, with respect, with dignity,

00:54:15.000 --> 00:54:19.000
and in a righteous fashion, I'm not gonna be angry about anything.

00:54:19.000 --> 00:54:24.000
And I, I have to confess a story, another story here, because these things keep happening.

00:54:25.000 --> 00:54:30.000
There is one case that we've been working on, and in this, this particular case, the person is not...

00:54:32.000 --> 00:54:35.000
I was gonna say appropriate, but that sounds so odd.

00:54:35.000 --> 00:54:38.000
The person does not actually belong in our institution.

00:54:38.000 --> 00:54:43.000
The person is developmentally disabled, which means that this person was retarded since they were born.

00:54:44.000 --> 00:54:49.000
And the agency that is supposed to provide the care for this person has decided not to do so,

00:54:49.000 --> 00:54:56.000
and has left the patient in our institution, which is not a good thing for the, for that patient at all.

00:54:56.000 --> 00:55:01.000
And in going to the meetings with many people coming together to decide what to do with this

00:55:01.000 --> 00:55:03.000
other person, the other person not present, of course.

00:55:03.000 --> 00:55:05.000
How can we best provide service?

00:55:05.000 --> 00:55:10.000
It was clear that there was a lot of politics going on, and people were trying to avoid spending money,

00:55:10.000 --> 00:55:15.000
and so they were literally dumping the problem in one particular area.

00:55:15.000 --> 00:55:21.000
And after the first meeting, I, I remember driving back to, to the hospital, and I don't even remember the drive back.

00:55:21.000 --> 00:55:24.000
I was so incensed at what had happened.

00:55:24.000 --> 00:55:31.000
I was so incensed at the dishonesty, at the manipulation that I had, had witnessed and heard,

00:55:31.000 --> 00:55:34.000
and that this person could be so badly mistreated.

00:55:35.000 --> 00:55:40.000
It took me a couple of hours to get rid of what amounted to anger.

00:55:40.000 --> 00:55:46.000
I was furious that this person, who is poor, who cannot fend for himself, has been totally disregarded.

00:55:47.000 --> 00:55:50.000
And by the time the two hours was over, I thought,

00:55:50.000 --> 00:55:54.000
I started looking around, cause I was sure the (unintelligible) floor was gonna open up and I was gonna go through it.

00:55:54.000 --> 00:56:00.000
I'd wasted two hours being angry at something that is happening according to God's will and for a reason.

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:06.000
And the person that I was angry for is perfectly happy where they are, and perfectly well-provided.

00:56:07.000 --> 00:56:09.000
And in fact, they're still there.

00:56:09.000 --> 00:56:12.000
So, again, we keep learning these lessons.

00:56:12.000 --> 00:56:19.000
I wasted a lot of energy, and you can bet that not once during that two hours was I thinking about God.

00:56:19.000 --> 00:56:22.000
It wasn't until I did think about God that the whole thing went away.

00:56:23.000 --> 00:56:25.000
And I had to be sincerely repentant.

00:56:25.000 --> 00:56:30.000
So, when we least expect it, those things come up in our lives as, as much as we strive.

00:56:32.000 --> 00:56:35.000
It's really important to control our emotions.

00:56:35.000 --> 00:56:39.000
It's the thing that can take us off the path very quickly.

00:56:41.000 --> 00:56:44.000
[94:2] ... we unloaded your load ... . [94:3] One that burdened your back.

